WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.987
A Membership Is Not a Shortcut to Community. A membership

2
00:00:04.987 --> 00:00:09.974
is a promise about an ongoing relationship. If the promise

3
00:00:09.974 --> 00:00:14.961
is vague, the payment becomes the whole story. That is

4
00:00:14.961 --> 00:00:19.948
not a durable community model. Beacon separates three things that

5
00:00:19.948 --> 00:00:24.935
are often blurred together: voluntary support, a paid member experience,

6
00:00:24.935 --> 00:00:29.922
and B2B services. Each has a different purpose, access model,

7
00:00:29.922 --> 00:00:34.909
and expectation. Support is not an investment. Voluntary support helps

8
00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:39.896
sustain public work. It carries no ownership, return, or special

9
00:00:39.896 --> 00:00:44.883
influence. Membership is an access promise. A membership should have

10
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:49.870
a reliable rhythm, a clear benefit set, and boundaries that

11
00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:54.857
are easy to explain. It is not founder access, consulting,

12
00:00:54.857 --> 00:00:59.844
or a guaranteed outcome. Services solve explicit work problems. Beacon

13
00:00:59.844 --> 00:01:04.831
Labs belongs in a separate conversation when an organization has

14
00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:09.818
a defined operating need and wants a scoped professional engagement.

15
00:01:09.818 --> 00:01:14.805
The strongest membership begins after a free publishing rhythm has

16
00:01:14.805 --> 00:01:19.792
already earned trust. Build the relationship first; then make the

17
00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:21.288
access promise clear.
